 ## Background
-The framework was introduced by S. Raman, O. Mishchenko, and R. Crawfis from the Department of Computer Science at The Ohio State University in 2008 [S1]. It builds on previous research on segmenting and rendering volumes, aiming to bring the power and ease of use found in 2D paint applications (like Photoshop) to volume rendering [S1]. The system architecture is described in detail in a technical report [MRC08], cited within the primary source [S1].
+The framework was presented by S. Raman, O. Mishchenko, and R. Crawfis from the Department of Computer Science at The Ohio State University [S1]. It was published in 2008 in the proceedings of Volume Graphics (VG) [S1]. The work builds on previous research on segmenting and rendering volumes and examines a new system architecture that allows digital artists and technical illustrators to leverage the layer concept from paint packages like Photoshop [S1]. The system architecture is detailed in a technical report [MRC08] referenced in the source [S1].
 
